WEBVTT

00:01.010 --> 00:03.050
<i>Please insert coins.</i>

00:04.620 --> 00:07.730
Okay, the magic energy flow is normal.

00:07.990 --> 00:10.830
And we're linked to the transfer 
circle on the other end.

00:08.530 --> 00:12.100
<i>Boxxo, this might be none of my business,</i>

00:10.830 --> 00:14.930
Director Bear, I'm done checking 
the circle. It's usable.

00:12.100 --> 00:15.280
<i>but I'll relay your words if 
you wish to speak with Lammis.</i>

00:15.680 --> 00:20.240
<i>It's true that I could talk with Lammis 
all I want, if I rely on Kikoyu...</i>

00:20.590 --> 00:21.900
<i>Thank-s, n-o.</i>

00:21.900 --> 00:23.440
<i>I see.</i>

00:23.440 --> 00:26.680
<i>Forgive me for being intrusive.</i>

00:26.680 --> 00:28.990
<i>I-s o-k-a-y, thank-s.</i>

00:29.280 --> 00:33.260
<i>But yeah, I want to talk to Lammis 
on my own the first time.</i>

00:34.060 --> 00:36.260
There, success.

00:36.820 --> 00:39.380
Okay, let's do this in order.

00:39.380 --> 00:41.220
We can start with Kikoyu's group.

00:41.220 --> 00:43.520
All right. Thank you.

00:48.020 --> 00:49.740
And lastly, us.

00:49.740 --> 00:50.570
Yeah.

00:50.570 --> 00:51.780
I'm activating it.

00:51.780 --> 00:52.490
Go ahead.

00:52.490 --> 00:53.910
<i>Hello there.</i>

00:55.000 --> 00:57.360
Huh? What was that?

00:58.080 --> 01:00.200
<i>Huh?! Why's there red light?!</i>

01:00.200 --> 01:03.460
What's going on?! I couldn't 
find anything wrong!

01:03.460 --> 01:06.080
No! I don't want to be 
apart from Boxxo anymore!

01:06.080 --> 01:08.850
<i>I don't want us to be 
separated anymore either!</i>

01:08.850 --> 01:11.690
<i>If we could at least all 
stay in one group...</i>

01:11.690 --> 01:12.600
<i>I know!</i>

01:12.600 --> 01:13.920
<i>Activate barrier!</i>

01:13.920 --> 01:17.960
<i>Please, send us all to the same place!</i>

01:20.100 --> 01:22.970
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:25.400 --> 01:27.270
<i>On the outside, a rectangular steel box.</i>

01:27.270 --> 01:29.270
<i>Hidden within is a human soul!</i>

01:29.270 --> 01:34.620
<i>In a world of wonder, I go to and fro 
on the back of my partner Lammis!</i>

01:30.360 --> 01:36.240
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:34.620 --> 01:37.130
<i>I am Boxxo! Hello there!</i>

01:37.130 --> 01:38.830
<i>That means "yes"!</i>

02:53.110 --> 02:56.940
<b>The Dark Forest Stratum</b>

02:58.510 --> 03:01.550
Boxxo! Hulemy! Thank goodness!

03:01.550 --> 03:02.700
Y-Yeah.

03:02.700 --> 03:05.060
<i>Okay, we're all together.</i>

03:05.420 --> 03:08.820
<i>I've never seen this room before.</i>

03:08.820 --> 03:10.250
What's going on here?!

03:10.250 --> 03:12.450
There was nothing wrong 
with the transfer circle!

03:12.450 --> 03:15.840
And everybody besides us 
went through no problem!

03:15.840 --> 03:18.960
Hulemy, I might have the wrong idea,

03:18.960 --> 03:23.370
but I think red light was coming from 
on top of Boxxo when we transferred.

03:23.370 --> 03:23.840
<i>Huh?</i>

03:28.860 --> 03:30.600
So that's it.

03:30.600 --> 03:34.710
A malfunction spell had been cast 
on Boxxo, not the transfer circle.

03:34.710 --> 03:36.030
What do you mean?

03:36.030 --> 03:39.640
There's a damn magic 
symbol stuck to his top.

03:39.640 --> 03:41.740
I'll go ahead and get rid of it.

03:41.740 --> 03:43.060
<i>My top?</i>

03:43.060 --> 03:45.030
<i>Oh! That's when it happened!</i>

03:45.370 --> 03:47.290
<i>He really got us good!</i>

03:47.290 --> 03:50.790
<i>What a troublemaker to have as an enemy.</i>

03:50.790 --> 03:53.790
Now, <i>next</i> time it won't malfunction.

03:54.250 --> 03:59.020
<i>Seems we have to wait a few days for the 
transfer circle's magic power to recharge.</i>

03:59.020 --> 04:01.470
This is the seventh stratum.

04:01.470 --> 04:04.750
Um, that's the Dark Forest stratum?

04:04.750 --> 04:09.390
I hear it's a pretty dangerous place, 
inhabited by lots of plant monsters.

04:09.390 --> 04:12.890
Although from the look of things, 
nothing's been destroyed.

04:14.290 --> 04:17.300
<i>Why's a tree growing right 
in front of the entrance?</i>

04:17.300 --> 04:19.570
<i>And the way it's shaped, it's like...</i>

04:19.570 --> 04:22.070
Doesn't it look like a person?

04:22.570 --> 04:27.800
I've heard there are monsters on this 
stratum that turn people into trees.

04:27.800 --> 04:31.850
It's bad news for women, children,
and elderly who can't put up a fight.

04:32.200 --> 04:35.450
<i>It's hard to look at them, hearing that.</i>

04:36.280 --> 04:37.700
Someone must be here!

04:37.700 --> 04:39.050
Over there!

04:44.550 --> 04:46.600
I'll deal with the carrot fiends!

04:53.230 --> 04:55.700
Sometimes their bodily fluids are harmful.

04:55.700 --> 04:58.310
If you get any on your boots, 
give them to me later!

04:58.310 --> 05:00.520
I'll help out!

05:01.980 --> 05:03.680
Your assistance is appreciated.

05:03.900 --> 05:05.490
Boxxo!

05:05.820 --> 05:07.110
I've been waiting for you!

05:07.110 --> 05:08.970
Food! Food!

05:07.480 --> 05:09.430
<i>"Boxxo!" "Boxxo!" "Boxxo!" "Boxxo!"</i>

05:09.430 --> 05:11.320
<i>Shui, calm down!</i>

05:10.280 --> 05:13.040
<b>Fried chicken
Grilled rice balls
Pasta with cream sauce
Hamburger combo
Hot dog
French fries
Imagawayaki
Yakisoba
Takoyaki</b>

05:18.670 --> 05:21.260
So good!

05:20.250 --> 05:23.670
Really! It's wonderful to have meat again!

05:22.260 --> 05:25.940
I've had enough of veggies. 
This fatty meat is the best!

05:23.670 --> 05:26.280
This place is naturally 
abundant and full of fields.

05:26.280 --> 05:30.850
There are vegetables aplenty, 
but meat, not so much.

05:30.850 --> 05:33.560
<i>No wonder they're wolfing it down.</i>

05:33.560 --> 05:35.350
Mishuel isn't here?

05:35.350 --> 05:39.320
Right, only Shui and I were sent here.

05:39.320 --> 05:40.450
<i>Ah, okay.</i>

05:40.450 --> 05:44.070
<i>Well, with Mishuel's strength,
he's probably fine no matter where he went.</i>

05:44.070 --> 05:48.830
But the houses haven't been destroyed, 
despite the monster assault.

05:49.120 --> 05:53.860
The monsters of this stratum are extremely 
reluctant to harm vegetation.

05:53.860 --> 05:56.570
Even in the case of felled trees.

05:56.570 --> 06:01.840
That must make them really mad when 
you cut down trees to build a house.

06:02.150 --> 06:03.300
That it does.

06:03.300 --> 06:06.580
Apparently, you must go to great pains 
here to cut down even just one.

06:06.580 --> 06:10.090
Were those trees in the 
village people after all?

06:10.360 --> 06:11.130
Yes.

06:11.130 --> 06:14.170
Those are elderlies, women, children, etc.

06:14.170 --> 06:18.590
who inhaled the stratum lord's pollen 
during a previous monster attack.

06:18.880 --> 06:22.240
I'm surprised anyone survived 
a stratum lord showing up.

06:22.240 --> 06:23.370
Did they defeat it?

06:23.370 --> 06:26.970
Oh no, they simply drove it away with fire.

06:26.970 --> 06:30.600
But they only use it as a threat,
for fear it could burn down the village.

06:30.600 --> 06:34.990
Oh yeah, I do recall fire 
being banned on this stratum.

06:34.990 --> 06:36.630
Indeed it is.

06:36.630 --> 06:43.250
They could easily defeat it with fire, but the 
trees of this stratum are especially flammable.

06:43.250 --> 06:47.080
The people who turned into 
trees, they won't turn back?

06:47.080 --> 06:49.710
I hear they will, if the 
stratum lord is defeated.

06:49.710 --> 06:50.950
Oh, okay!

06:50.950 --> 06:56.490
But, how are you supposed to find 
that stratum lord in this forest?

06:56.490 --> 07:00.150
Ah, simply finding it is easy.

07:00.730 --> 07:02.110
That's it there.

07:02.910 --> 07:03.910
<i>What?!</i>

07:03.910 --> 07:05.370
<i>That's way too big!</i>

07:05.370 --> 07:07.900
<i>It might be taller than a skyscraper!</i>

07:07.900 --> 07:11.400
If something that big moved around, the 
forest trees would get knocked down.

07:11.400 --> 07:14.610
I suppose that's one of the lord's powers.

07:14.610 --> 07:17.660
When it does move,
the trees get out of the way.

07:18.010 --> 07:21.310
<i>A stratum lord that can control 
plants in a forest, eh?</i>

07:21.310 --> 07:23.920
<i>That wouldn't be easy to deal with.</i>

07:23.920 --> 07:26.800
Well, let's talk some more tomorrow.

07:26.800 --> 07:29.770
You see the state everyone's in today.

07:29.770 --> 07:31.920
I can't eat any more.

07:31.920 --> 07:35.300
<i>I'd say Shui won't be 
of any use for a while.</i>

07:35.730 --> 07:38.730
<i>We'll be the ones to stand guard today.</i>

07:41.320 --> 07:45.950
You know, it's been forever since 
it was just you and me like this.

07:45.950 --> 07:48.930
<i>It sure has been, now that you mention it.</i>

07:48.930 --> 07:51.920
You might get mad if I say this now,

07:52.520 --> 07:56.320
but I get the feeling I can 
do anything if I'm with you.

07:56.320 --> 07:58.700
<i>I feel that way too, Lammis.</i>

07:58.700 --> 08:01.200
<i>Y-ea. Thank-s.</i>

08:02.060 --> 08:04.390
"Thanks" is an odd thing to say.

08:05.100 --> 08:08.710
<i>Huh? Wh-What's this bittersweet vibe?</i>

08:10.260 --> 08:11.810
<i>Whoa, Lammis?!</i>

08:11.810 --> 08:13.210
<i>Hold on a minute!</i>

08:13.210 --> 08:15.980
<i>Um, what's happening here?</i>

08:15.980 --> 08:18.980
<i>Are you telling me this is the 
start of an outrageous rom-com</i>

08:18.980 --> 08:23.480
<i>between an inorganic object and a girl?!</i>

08:25.350 --> 08:28.410
Right, we're on watch. Too bad.

08:29.200 --> 08:31.520
<i>We've got to take it seriously, yeah.</i>

08:31.520 --> 08:32.650
Huh.

08:32.900 --> 08:35.620
So lately, you've been 
eating these monsters?

08:35.620 --> 08:36.690
That's right.

08:36.690 --> 08:40.400
The vegetable monsters here taste 
pretty good, in their own way.

08:42.530 --> 08:47.500
Besides, there's plenty of lumber,
so thankfully I won't be running out of arrows.

08:47.500 --> 08:48.520
Shui!

08:48.790 --> 08:51.290
I brought you more arrows.

08:51.290 --> 08:52.560
Thanks!

08:52.560 --> 08:53.290
You got it!

08:53.520 --> 08:57.430
The one with the oft-mentioned Boxxo on her 
back must be the Blessing of Might girl.

08:58.140 --> 08:59.680
The name's Lammis.

08:59.680 --> 09:02.550
Oh, okay. Sorry 'bout that.

09:02.550 --> 09:06.050
I hear you fight bare-handed, Lammis.

09:06.050 --> 09:07.500
Yeah, that's right.

09:07.500 --> 09:10.160
What a waste of your Blessing of Might.

09:10.160 --> 09:11.740
Come over to my shop.

09:11.740 --> 09:14.070
I'll find you a good weapon.

09:14.760 --> 09:18.160
<i>Oh! So this is an otherworldly weapons shop!</i>

09:18.160 --> 09:21.000
But I don't need any weapons.

09:21.000 --> 09:22.470
It can't hurt to look.

09:22.470 --> 09:26.330
He said you could have whichever you 
want as thanks for Boxxo's food.

09:27.550 --> 09:29.880
<i>I knew there'd be all kinds here!</i>

09:29.880 --> 09:33.450
I'm surprised to see some 
with magic stones built in.

09:33.450 --> 09:36.780
What do you think of my shop?

09:36.780 --> 09:38.540
Feel free to look around.

09:38.980 --> 09:40.290
What's this?

09:40.290 --> 09:41.370
Oh, that one?

09:41.370 --> 09:45.770
It's water-repellent, good in the hot 
or cold, and it performs wonderfully.

09:45.770 --> 09:49.850
But it's also flashy, and well,
it's not for sale.

09:50.500 --> 09:52.390
What do you think, Boxxo?

09:52.390 --> 09:54.190
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

09:54.190 --> 09:56.870
Was that a compliment?

09:56.870 --> 09:57.740
<i>Y-ea.</i>

09:58.560 --> 09:59.730
Thanks.

09:59.730 --> 10:02.470
<i>I'm really surprised by 
how good it looks on her.</i>

10:02.470 --> 10:05.480
<i>But then, just about anything 
would look good on Lammis.</i>

10:05.480 --> 10:08.420
<i>I know, let's try getting 
him to sell it to us later.</i>

10:08.880 --> 10:12.350
Now then, this one's a type of magic item.

10:12.350 --> 10:14.880
They get heavier the moment you pick one up.

10:14.880 --> 10:16.720
Measuring stones, eh?

10:16.720 --> 10:19.560
That's a pretty unusual magic 
item you've got there.

10:19.560 --> 10:22.380
Sounds like you know your stuff.

10:22.380 --> 10:24.380
Go on, try it out.

10:24.380 --> 10:26.120
Oh, that's light.

10:26.120 --> 10:28.020
You make it look easy.

10:28.020 --> 10:29.770
Want to try holding it, Hulemy?

10:29.770 --> 10:31.400
Sure, hand it ov—

10:32.500 --> 10:34.850
Lammis! Take it! Take it!

10:34.400 --> 10:35.250
Okay!

10:35.250 --> 10:38.160
<i>Looks like that was a close call.</i>

10:38.440 --> 10:41.330
Okay, let's skip over one. 
How about number three?

10:42.470 --> 10:44.030
S-Seriously?

10:44.030 --> 10:46.410
Sure, it's still totally light.

10:46.410 --> 10:48.920
All right, how about the one at the end?

10:49.930 --> 10:52.790
It's about as heavy as Boxxo!

10:52.790 --> 10:54.360
Really?!

10:55.590 --> 10:56.970
This is incredible!

10:56.970 --> 10:58.670
I didn't think you were <i>this</i> strong!

10:58.670 --> 11:03.310
Right! I'm gonna make you 
your ultimate weapon!

11:03.310 --> 11:04.420
<i>Oh!</i>

11:04.420 --> 11:06.940
<i>This weapons merchant guy 
is practically on fire!</i>

11:06.940 --> 11:08.170
You really want to?

11:08.170 --> 11:10.270
Oh yeah! I'm on it!

11:11.860 --> 11:16.110
<i>You know, we have yet to meet 
the director of this stratum.</i>

11:16.110 --> 11:18.870
<i>Even though we dropped in at the 
Hunters Association fairly soon</i>

11:18.870 --> 11:20.810
<i>when we went to other strata.</i>

11:20.810 --> 11:22.190
<i>He-y.</i>

11:22.600 --> 11:27.640
<i>D-o you n-o th-e d-i-r-e-k-t-er h-ea-r?</i>

11:27.640 --> 11:31.730
Director Dark?
No, I guess I haven't met him.

11:31.730 --> 11:33.330
Do you know what he's like?

11:36.620 --> 11:38.960
Well, let's see.

11:39.270 --> 11:44.080
I would say he's cheerful and fun?
A good fit for this stratum's director.

11:44.080 --> 11:46.590
He's not a bad guy.

11:48.020 --> 11:50.090
<i>What's with those reactions?</i>

11:50.530 --> 11:54.990
If you're curious about the director, 
this might be good timing.

11:56.080 --> 11:57.820
Hey, nice to meetcha!

11:57.820 --> 11:59.730
You can call me Director Dark, if ya like!

11:59.730 --> 12:03.060
I mean, I'd be thrilled if 
ya just remembered my face.

12:03.060 --> 12:05.660
But then, what's to remember 
when it's completely dark?!

12:05.660 --> 12:07.320
That's the part when you laugh.

12:07.320 --> 12:10.940
Darkness fiend's my race,
and "darkness" sounds all impressive,

12:10.940 --> 12:13.120
but my vibe's actually about 
cheerfulness and liveliness!

12:13.120 --> 12:17.930
I might be a darkness fiend, but don't worry,
I won't say anything gloomy!

12:17.930 --> 12:20.010
My days are all hectic and messy...

12:20.010 --> 12:21.230
Think I'll have a seat.

12:21.230 --> 12:25.250
...but it's my opinion that as director, 
I've got to do my best to be dignified.

12:25.250 --> 12:28.970
Oh yeah, you guys are from 
Clearflow Lake stratum, right?

12:28.970 --> 12:30.840
How is Director Bear doin'?

12:30.840 --> 12:33.030
I bet he keeps busy, too!

12:33.030 --> 12:36.090
Doesn't he say every day is just 
a total <i>bear</i> to get through?

12:36.090 --> 12:40.270
I myself do desk work, farm work, late-night 
patrols, and I even sweep chimneys!

12:38.810 --> 12:41.200
<i>He talks like a manzai performer,</i>

12:40.270 --> 12:42.680
I mean, look at me, I'm pitch black!

12:41.200 --> 12:43.830
<i>and this hail of bad jokes is killing me!</i>

12:43.920 --> 12:48.360
I would say he's cheerful and fun?
A good fit for this stratum's director...

12:48.360 --> 12:50.620
He's not a bad guy.

12:50.620 --> 12:54.730
<i>I wondered why those two didn't 
come along to introduce us.</i>

12:54.730 --> 12:58.740
No need to be nervous and 
stiff as a board, Boxxo.

12:58.740 --> 13:00.720
Oh, I guess you're always this stiff.

13:01.880 --> 13:08.240
From what I'm told,
Boxxo dispenses unusual food and drink.

13:08.240 --> 13:10.520
I don't suppose I'd mind getting 
to try something myself.

13:10.520 --> 13:13.420
<i>I want to refuse,
but this guy's a director...</i>

13:13.420 --> 13:15.510
<i>I guess I have to be nice to him.</i>

13:15.730 --> 13:17.150
<b>Kocha Kadan</b>

13:17.140 --> 13:20.430
Ya really can make stuff 
float through the air.

13:20.430 --> 13:22.310
Wow, that's somethin', there.

13:22.310 --> 13:24.450
Now, don't mind if I do.

13:26.500 --> 13:27.970
That's tasty stuff.

13:27.970 --> 13:30.130
More than I'd expect from sweet tea.

13:30.130 --> 13:32.910
Now all I need to go with 
it's a sweet-tea pie!

13:32.910 --> 13:34.120
<i>Enough!</i>

13:34.120 --> 13:38.040
<i>I might have to listen to dad jokes 
forever if I don't do something.</i>

13:38.040 --> 13:41.010
<i>There must be some way to outdo him...</i>

13:41.010 --> 13:42.240
<i>Oh yeah, that!</i>

13:42.680 --> 13:44.240
<i>Form change!</i>

13:43.160 --> 13:45.510
What's with the light show?

13:44.780 --> 13:48.170
<i>A manzai vending machine!</i>

13:45.630 --> 13:47.180
<b>Vending Venue of Laughs</b>

13:45.630 --> 13:47.180
<b>Hot Coffee
Café au Lait
Lemon Tea
Milk Tea
Hot Cocoa
Green Tea
Iced Coffee
Iced Café au Lait
Iced Tea
Iced Lemon Tea
Iced Milk Tea
Iced Cocoa
Iced Milk
Chilled Green Tea
Your Smile ¥0</b>

13:47.780 --> 13:49.930
What's this, now?!

13:48.330 --> 13:49.210
<i>Hello.</i>

13:49.210 --> 13:50.880
<i>How is everybody?</i>

13:50.880 --> 13:54.120
<i>What a big audience!
Thanks for comin' to see us.</i>

13:54.120 --> 13:58.060
<i>From the end, we've got a pretty girl, 
pretty girl, skip that one, pretty girl.</i>

13:58.060 --> 13:59.190
<i>Cut that out!</i>

13:59.190 --> 14:02.030
<i>Get this, my ma can't remember 
her favorite novel.</i>

14:02.030 --> 14:04.510
<i>I'll think of it for ya. Describe it.</i>

14:04.510 --> 14:06.130
<i>The main character goes to another world.</i>

14:05.020 --> 14:07.340
Wh-What is this?

14:06.130 --> 14:09.460
<i>Oh, that makes it an isekai story.
That was easy.</i>

14:09.230 --> 14:12.950
<i>Watch and learn from the old school!</i>

14:09.460 --> 14:11.690
<i>But Ma says it's based on a real story.</i>

14:11.690 --> 14:14.110
<i>Nah, can't be. It's the exact opposite.</i>

14:14.110 --> 14:16.400
<i>Pa says it must be a fortune-telling 
book, a porn book, or a cookbook.</i>

14:16.400 --> 14:17.390
<i>That can't be right.</i>

14:17.390 --> 14:18.560
<i>What's yer pa know anyway?</i>

14:18.560 --> 14:19.450
<i>Forget about it.</i>

14:19.450 --> 14:21.470
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

14:23.290 --> 14:25.460
Thanks for taking the time to come today.

14:25.870 --> 14:29.420
<i>Hopefully, this calms things 
down at least a little.</i>

14:29.970 --> 14:33.970
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
 I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

14:31.210 --> 14:33.100
<i>Vending Machine Two...</i>

14:33.100 --> 14:33.970
<i>Huh?</i>

14:34.740 --> 14:37.520
We'll fell some trees to make a path.

14:37.520 --> 14:40.070
If the monsters seem too dangerous, 
we'll come right back.

14:40.070 --> 14:43.400
Our goal this time is to measure 
how powerful the enemies are.

14:45.670 --> 14:47.240
Here comes a big welcome.

14:47.560 --> 14:49.400
Shall we deal with them first?

14:49.400 --> 14:50.980
<i>Deal</i> you have to ask?

14:52.730 --> 14:54.340
<i>That's how he comes across,</i>

14:54.340 --> 14:58.750
<i>but Director Dark apparently used to 
be in the same group as Director Bear.</i>

14:58.750 --> 15:01.500
<i>He's probably plenty capable.</i>

15:04.540 --> 15:07.290
I better put vegetables 
on my <i>chop</i>ping list. {note}

15:07.290 --> 15:10.290
<i>He's saying something, but I'll 
pretend I didn't hear it.</i>

15:14.920 --> 15:17.180
Lammis, there are less enemies now.

15:17.180 --> 15:18.730
Please remove some trees.

15:18.730 --> 15:19.680
Okay.

15:31.280 --> 15:32.910
<i>That's an amazing sight.</i>

15:32.910 --> 15:35.000
I'm just getting started!

15:36.040 --> 15:39.570
Lammis! Let's call it a day and head back!

15:39.570 --> 15:40.540
Okay!

15:40.540 --> 15:46.040
<i>Thus did we spend a few days clearing trees 
and extending the path through the forest.</i>

15:52.050 --> 15:55.310
We've come this far, but still no movement.

15:55.310 --> 15:59.020
It might be faster just to 
look for the commander.

15:59.020 --> 16:02.100
Oh, here you are. I've been looking for you.

16:02.100 --> 16:03.880
Botan, Kuroyata.

16:03.880 --> 16:06.810
And Director Bear and Kikoyu! Everyone!

16:06.810 --> 16:08.760
Whoa, how'd you do it?

16:08.760 --> 16:11.810
I thought the transfer circle wouldn't 
be usable for two or three days.

16:11.810 --> 16:13.820
You're asking how we got here?

16:13.820 --> 16:16.800
The flow of magic power 
seems to have settled down,

16:16.800 --> 16:21.820
so I directed it from the other side 
to activate the transfer circle.

16:21.820 --> 16:25.950
Not bad. It would take someone 
with your skill to do it.

16:25.950 --> 16:28.430
I didn't grow old for nothin'.

16:28.430 --> 16:30.610
It's been a long time, ma'am.

16:30.950 --> 16:33.640
Well, well, it's the girl with the appetite.

16:33.640 --> 16:35.220
Shui is your name, yes?

16:35.480 --> 16:37.840
I'm sure that mess with the 
captain was difficult.

16:37.840 --> 16:40.340
Don't worry, it's behind me now.

16:40.340 --> 16:42.630
Are we there yet?

16:42.100 --> 16:44.570
Is it time to eat?

16:43.730 --> 16:45.320
Morning already?

16:44.280 --> 16:48.360
Shirley said lack of sleep 
is the archenemy of beauty.

16:48.360 --> 16:50.820
<i>Even the Band of Gluttons is with them.</i>

16:50.820 --> 16:54.160
<i>Now Team Traveling Zoo is complete!</i>

16:54.160 --> 16:56.620
<i>It's all the soothing animal 
time you could want.</i>

16:57.670 --> 17:01.330
Time to face the music, 
and go see Black-Black.

17:02.710 --> 17:04.280
Ow, ow, ow!

17:04.280 --> 17:06.660
My back pain just flared up.

17:05.320 --> 17:07.340
Are you okay, Gramps?

17:07.340 --> 17:10.250
I'm sorry, I need to tend to him.

17:09.620 --> 17:11.480
You're coming with me.

17:11.480 --> 17:14.460
Dealing with him alone is exhausting.

17:14.460 --> 17:16.790
<i>Ah, he means Director Dark.</i>

17:17.090 --> 17:18.560
Let's head back.

17:19.300 --> 17:21.060
Yeah...

17:21.400 --> 17:23.980
Kikoyu, take care of you-know-what.

17:23.980 --> 17:25.680
Yes, I will.

17:25.680 --> 17:28.180
<i>What's that in reference to?</i>

17:28.780 --> 17:30.080
<i>Boxxo.</i>

17:30.080 --> 17:32.410
<i>Bear asked me for a favor.</i>

17:32.410 --> 17:34.060
<i>Would you mind helping?</i>

17:34.060 --> 17:35.380
<i>A favor?</i>

17:36.070 --> 17:40.600
<i>Are the people currently in this 
village everyone on this stratum?</i>

17:36.240 --> 17:42.080
<b>Family Market</b>

17:40.600 --> 17:41.760
<i>That's right.</i>

17:41.760 --> 17:43.870
<i>It's about time for me to distribute food,</i>

17:42.080 --> 17:45.660
<b>Family Market</b>

17:43.870 --> 17:45.660
<i>so I think they're all going to gather.</i>

17:45.890 --> 17:51.120
<i>Then as we discussed,
I will hand out your products.</i>

17:51.120 --> 17:52.410
<i>Hello there.</i>

17:52.410 --> 17:54.000
Here you are.

17:52.420 --> 17:52.670
<b></b>Deluxe Grilled Rice Balls

17:52.670 --> 17:52.800
<b></b>Deluxe Grilled Rice Balls

17:52.800 --> 17:54.420
<b></b>Deluxe Grilled Rice Balls

17:54.380 --> 17:56.610
Um, your name's Kikoyu?

17:56.610 --> 17:57.960
Thanks.

17:59.920 --> 18:01.940
Thanks, little miss.

18:04.180 --> 18:05.430
Here you are.

18:05.730 --> 18:08.190
<i>I've figured out what Kikoyu has in mind.</i>

18:09.520 --> 18:10.770
Here you are.

18:14.110 --> 18:16.350
<i>Right! I'll record her face.</i>

18:16.730 --> 18:20.100
<i>Kikoyu was reading minds as she 
handed over the box lunches,</i>

18:20.100 --> 18:22.120
<i>in order to search for the commander.</i>

18:22.120 --> 18:24.910
This person is the Netherlord's commander.

18:25.980 --> 18:28.350
That's one of my hunters!

18:28.350 --> 18:32.790
That youngster's been working hard here on 
this stratum, and I had high hopes for her!

18:32.790 --> 18:35.950
I had no idea she was working 
for the Netherlord!

18:35.950 --> 18:37.090
I see.

18:37.090 --> 18:40.800
But we don't know whether she was hiding
it all along or was persuaded to defect.

18:40.800 --> 18:43.540
Now, what to do next?

18:43.540 --> 18:46.610
<i>We should get information out 
of her immediately, but...</i>

18:47.230 --> 18:50.180
<i>Oh, I know. We have just the man for it.</i>

18:50.770 --> 18:51.560
<b>Kocha Kadan</b>

18:51.550 --> 18:53.960
<i>H-ea c-a-n d-ou i-t.</i>

18:54.570 --> 18:55.320
Huh?

18:55.320 --> 18:57.070
That is an option.

18:57.070 --> 19:00.730
Hevee, we'd like you to arrest 
and question the commander.

19:00.730 --> 19:02.320
Would you mind?

19:02.320 --> 19:05.580
Ah, I see. Yes, that's fine.

19:05.580 --> 19:10.330
I can use hallucinations to get information, 
or perhaps affect her emotionally.

19:10.330 --> 19:14.660
Well, you might wanna leave 
the arrest up to me.

19:14.660 --> 19:19.780
This scandal happened on my watch, 
so I need to set things right.

19:23.240 --> 19:27.310
<i>I couldn't read his expression, but 
I could sense he was really angry.</i>

19:27.790 --> 19:31.530
<i>As director, I imagine he 
wants to clean up this mess.</i>

19:31.530 --> 19:33.490
Uh, where can I find her?

19:33.490 --> 19:34.990
D'oh!

19:36.130 --> 19:37.870
Okay, here she comes.

19:41.860 --> 19:46.630
This room's well soundproofed, too.
Nobody's gonna hear this.

19:46.630 --> 19:48.610
Well, take it from here.

19:48.610 --> 19:53.100
I will use my sensory manipulation to 
deactivate her sense of touch and pain,

19:53.100 --> 19:55.150
and make her believe she is dreaming.

19:55.150 --> 19:59.410
I will alter her vision to 
make her see the Netherlord.

19:59.410 --> 20:03.630
But she will be able to hear,
so please refrain from speaking.

20:04.280 --> 20:08.630
If her sense of touch is disabled,
she won't know if someone touches her.

20:12.230 --> 20:15.430
I am speaking to you in your dream.

20:16.330 --> 20:18.770
Can you tell who I am?

20:18.770 --> 20:20.350
The Netherlord.

20:20.350 --> 20:23.850
<i>Oh, he must appear to be the Netherlord.</i>

20:24.220 --> 20:29.860
Then recount for me the circumstances 
under which you began working for me.

20:29.860 --> 20:31.020
Yes, sir.

20:31.020 --> 20:35.740
About two months ago, you 
appeared before me as a human,

20:35.740 --> 20:40.830
and said if I obeyed you, you'd give me 
enough money to pay off my gambling debt

20:40.830 --> 20:45.100
and live the rest of my 
life without working.

20:45.100 --> 20:47.330
What did I tell you to do?

20:48.010 --> 20:51.010
While helping to defend as a hunter,

20:51.010 --> 20:55.010
I would use this ring to order 
the monsters to attack.

20:55.010 --> 20:57.770
Is that all you can remember?

20:57.770 --> 21:04.100
About two weeks ago, I met with the newly 
recruited members of the Menagerie of Fools.

21:04.730 --> 21:09.780
They seemed to be looking for someone, but they 
left as soon as they realized they weren't here.

21:09.780 --> 21:12.850
<i>So, the captain and crew 
dropped by this stratum.</i>

21:12.850 --> 21:16.430
<i>They were probably looking for the 
two remaining Menagerie members.</i>

21:18.030 --> 21:22.550
One last thing. Could you take off 
those boots and show them to me?

21:22.550 --> 21:25.060
<i>Hey, what're you saying as the Netherlord?!</i>

21:25.060 --> 21:27.490
Um, my boots?

21:27.930 --> 21:31.720
For some strange reason, I'm 
finding it hard to move.

21:31.720 --> 21:34.320
Then I shall carefully remove them myself,

21:34.320 --> 21:38.180
so that the scent gradually 
makes its way out of—

21:39.710 --> 21:41.680
D-Director...

21:41.680 --> 21:45.200
You've always had a problem with gambling.

21:45.690 --> 21:49.130
But I believed what you said.

21:49.130 --> 21:53.690
When I loaned you money before,
you said you'd never gamble again.

21:53.690 --> 21:55.960
I really did believe you.

21:57.040 --> 21:59.950
<i>That takes care of the commander.</i>

22:00.460 --> 22:04.400
<i>All that's left is to turn all 
those trees back into people.</i>

23:35.010 --> 23:37.050
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.090
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.090
<b>Conflagration</b>

23:37.880 --> 23:40.060
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>
